  "patch_sha256": "82579127fc150bbd7943fa0448a355d71b6f802c27002ab3f1de00f69bef7243",
  "physical_verified": false,
  "combined_bundle_promoted": false,
  "scope": "msm_ext_display, sync_fence (spec fences), msm_hfi_core (canoe defconfigs) on android18-7.3; msm-mmrm in source-spec-mmrm.json",
  "reviewed_changes": [
    "sync_fence: 7.3 dma_fence_array_create() lost signal_on_any; the 6.12 init only set num_pending=1 for 'any', which 7.3 callbacks still honour - set after create, before signaling is enabled (QEMU: ANY/ALL/default verified; negative control without it fails ANY)",
    "sync_fence: fence->lock -> dma_fence_spinlock(); bind takes it irqsave (dma_fence_array signals from hardirq irq_work; the vendor plain spin_lock is a lockdep-reported deadlock, also latent on 6.12); dma_fence_enable_sw_signaling -> dma_fence_enable_signaling",
    "msm_hfi_core: all canoe srcs incl. firmware/irq/ssr (define_hfi_core.bzl); rproc_set_state inline stub as the vendor header gives canoe (no QCOM_Q6V5_PAS_SOCCP_V1; phone module imports nothing from qcom_q6v5_pas)",
    "function symbol sets match the phone modules (nm vs /proc/kallsyms) apart from inlining"
  ],
  "pending": [
    "display bring-up with msm_drm on the phone"
  ]
}
